     7	#   signoff.sh record <commit> --base BASE --rounds-at NOTED --date YYYY-MM-DD --quote TEXT
     8	#                     --codex-request FILE --codex FILE --kimi-request FILE --kimi FILE
     9	#                     --agy-request FILE --agy FILE
    10	#   signoff.sh verify <commit> --base BASE
    11	#
    12	# THE RECORD is the ref refs/owner-signoff/<full sha>, a parentless commit whose tree holds exactly
    13	# seven plain files: record.txt and, for each reviewer r in codex, kimi and agy, r-request.txt and
    14	# r.txt. The output is copied byte for byte. The request is copied verbatim after a structured first
    15	# line, `reviewed: <full sha>`, which `record` prepends to attest the commit reviewed. Thus a clone
    16	# that fetches the ref can check what each reviewer was asked and its output separately. record.txt
    17	# is `key: value` lines, each key once:
    18	#   signoff: owner
    19	#   commit: <the 40-hex SHA approved>
    20	#   date: YYYY-MM-DD
    21	#   quote: <the owner's words, verbatim; they name the commit by an unambiguous prefix of 7+ hex digits>
    22	#   rounds-at: <the 40-hex SHA of the commit whose scripts/review/review.sh note records the rounds used>
    23	#   request-codex: codex-request.txt <sha256>
    24	#   verdict-codex: codex.txt <sha256>
    25	#   request-kimi: kimi-request.txt <sha256>
    26	#   verdict-kimi: kimi.txt <sha256>
    27	#   request-agy: agy-request.txt <sha256>
    28	#   verdict-agy: agy.txt <sha256>
    29	# `record` builds the record, verifies it, and only then writes the ref locally; it pushes nothing
    30	# (push the ref to both remotes: the pre-push hook takes a refs/owner-signoff/* record in its
    31	# no-source-tree tier). Only the owner's recorded words go in a quote.
    32	#
    33	# THE CAP (R-0618) comes from the class of the member's diff against its base, classified by path,
    34	# the highest class present winning: docs and roadmap 2, scripts 3, compiler and spec 5; a path in no
    35	# class counts as compiler and spec. A sign-off qualifies only when the review rounds recorded on the
    36	# member's own commits reach that cap: `rounds-at` must be the commit itself or one of its ancestors
    37	# not on BASE, and carry a well-formed review.sh note (scripts/review/verify.sh: clean, findings or
    38	# blocked) whose round is at least the cap, whatever its verdict
    39	# (the cap counts rounds used: the other reviewers' rejections are why a branch reaches it).
    40	#
    41	# `verify` accepts the record only if the ref exists, the tree holds exactly those seven 100644 blobs,
    42	# every key is present once and well formed, `commit` is the commit asked about, the quote names it,
    43	# the cap was reached, and every file's sha256 is the recorded one. Each request's `reviewed:` line
